<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  T.EN reference-data extension library - companion to, NOT a replacement
  for or edit of, specs/semantics/equipment.rdf (the pinned, externally-owned
  PCA PLM equipment library, owl:versionInfo tracked against real PCA
  releases). See gold/vocab.py's module docstring for the TEN_RDL namespace
  this file populates, and gold_layer_spec.md's Workstream 1.5 / Cause C
  discussion for why this file exists at all.

  When to add a class here, vs. use the existing crosswalk/alias mechanism:
    - A real RDS/DEXPI code (or PostProc ComponentClass string) resolves,
      even loosely, to an existing PCA PLM class -> that's a crosswalk
      entry in rds_plm_crosswalk.json (match_type "close"), NOT a new class
      here. Most of Cause C's real gap is this case.
    - A real RDS/DEXPI code names a genuine physical/functional equipment
      or component type the PCA PLM library (specs/semantics/equipment.rdf)
      does not name precisely enough, confirmed by checking the real file
      directly (the same discipline this project already applies before
      calling anything "missing" from a reference library) -> that is what
      belongs here, as a new class under TEN_RDL.
    - A DEXPI drawing-continuation symbol, off-page connector, or other
      non-physical artifact -> belongs in neither place. It is not a
      component the PLM/RDL model classifies at all; use REJECT in
      confirm_cause_c_review.py instead of minting a class for it here.

  Namespace prefixes below are copied verbatim from the real equipment.rdf
  so the two files stay stylistically interoperable (skos:closeMatch back
  to a real RDS URI works exactly the same way here as it does there) -
  most of them are unused in this file today and only carried over for that
  consistency; trim ones you never use if that bothers you.

  Status: one real class populated - SteamTrap (below), subclassed under
  the real PCA Valve class (PCA_100004125, confirmed by David from his own
  copy of equipment.rdf on 2026-09-15).
-->
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://www.semanticweb.org/owl/owlapi/turtle#"
     xml:base="http://www.semanticweb.org/owl/owlapi/turtle"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:lis="http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/"
     xmlns:pca="http://data.posccaesar.org/rdl/"
     xmlns:rdl="http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/plm/rdl/"
     xmlns:ten="http://data.ten.com/rdl/">

    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://data.ten.com/rdl/ont/equipment-extension">
        <owl:versionInfo>0.3.0</owl:versionInfo>
        <rdfs:comment>T.EN reference-data extension to the PCA PLM equipment
library (specs/semantics/equipment.rdf). Project-owned; not a PCA-published
ontology. See this file's own header comment and gold/vocab.py's TEN_RDL
namespace documentation before adding classes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>

    <!--
      SteamTrap - first real class in this file (added per David's
      decision; see claude/ten_rdl_extension_design.md).

      Real evidence this is a genuine, established component class in this
      project, not an invented one:
        - silver/_recon/pidsys/refdata.py::_FALLBACK_BOUNDARY["trap"] =
          {"SteamTrap"} - one of the four real boundary-role sets the
          systemization walk reads.
        - systemization_spec.md §5.7 - "The steam trap belongs to the
          Steam system... The steam/condensate boundary is the first
          flange downstream of the steam trap."
        - data_specification.md §3.1 - "Steam Trap | Fitting /
          boundary-forming | Missing from source class list - see note"
          and the accompanying note: the validation drawing checked had no
          component classified as a steam trap, and "recognising Steam
          Trap as a class... is an open reference-data item."

      PCA parent confirmed 2026-09-15: David checked his own full copy of
      equipment.rdf and confirmed the real generic Valve class is
      PCA_100004125 (rdl: namespace, http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/plm/rdl/).
      SteamTrap is declared rdfs:subClassOf it below - a steam trap is a
      real physical/functional class the PCA library does not name
      precisely (no dedicated Steam Trap class exists there), but it is
      still a valve-family device, so it is wired into the real PLM
      hierarchy under its nearest real parent rather than left orphaned.
    -->
    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://data.ten.com/rdl/SteamTrap">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/plm/rdl/PCA_100004125"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A steam trap: the directional device that forms the
boundary between a Steam system and its Condensate system
(systemization_spec.md §5.7). Boundary role "trap" in the project's
reference data. Subclassed under the real PCA Valve class (PCA_100004125)
- confirmed by David from his own full copy of equipment.rdf on
2026-09-15, since this environment could not fetch far enough into that
file (246 classes) to confirm it independently.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Steam Trap</rdfs:label>
        <!-- Once you've confirmed the real DEXPI/PostProc RDS or
             ComponentClassURI this corresponds to on real data, add it
             here instead of (or alongside) a rds_plm_crosswalk.json entry:
        <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="http://sandbox.dexpi.org/rdl/SteamTrap"/>
        -->
    </owl:Class>

</rdf:RDF>
